    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup today, anchored by our strongest play, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries an elite efficiency score of 73.66. His massive boost is driven by an ideal matchup against Grant Holmes (4.71 xERA) and an advantageous platoon split that raises his baseline significantly. We are also leaning heavily on the table-setting ability of **Jacob Wilson** (59.39) and **Kyle Tucker** (59.83); while **Kyle Tucker** faces a tough arm in Bryan Woo, the wind blowing out at the stadium provides a critical edge to his power profile. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Jacob Wilson** are effectively the engine room for today\u2019s production, both benefiting from prime spots at the top of their respective orders.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final outfield slot, where **Luis Robert Jr.** (49.93) missed the cut in favor of the more efficient **Andy Pages** (57.00). While **Luis Robert Jr.** possesses the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base-starved 5x5 build, his aggressive negative platoon adjustment against Eury P\u00e9rez ultimately capped his projection. **Andy Pages** provides a safer floor and a superior order position, making him the logical choice to round out the outfield. We must monitor the status of **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Dominic Smith**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages** closely; with all lineups currently pending, the final efficiency scores remain fluid. Should any of these players move down in the order once official cards are posted, their projected values\u2014and our total output\u2014could shift significantly.",
